#AUTO 100
#NEEDED 0
# eMMC ADMA2 (DMA) read validation — issue 110m, the throughput half of
# fast storage and the thing that makes a full eMMC dump practical.
#
# Instead of the CPU hand-copying every word out of the controller FIFO
# (PIO), this hands the controller a descriptor — "move these bytes to
# this RAM address" — and lets it burst the data itself. emmc_read_blocks_dma
# (in src/012-emmc.c) does an ADMA2 + CMD18 multi-block read; emmc_verify_dma
# reads 8 blocks from the non-zero idbloader region (LBA 64) that way and
# fingerprints the first block.
#
# The go/no-go is the fingerprint: the DMA fingerprint must MATCH the PIO
# emmc_verify fingerprint (0xC4FBFA8B on this card), be non-zero, and carry
# rc 0, at each speed. That proves the descriptor path moves correct bytes.
# A mismatch / DATA ERROR / rc -10 (count) means the ADMA2 setup is wrong.
#
# Run at all three speeds so DMA correctness is isolated from speed mode:
#   PIO legacy (baseline)  -> DMA legacy
#   DMA at HS200
#   DMA at HS400  (the full-speed, CPU-free read the dump will use)
#
# Read-only, safe to re-run. Needs emmc_verify_dma + emmc_verify (engine 019).

CALL emmc_init
CALL emmc_verify
CALL emmc_verify_dma
CALL emmc_hs200
CALL emmc_verify_dma
CALL emmc_hs400
CALL emmc_verify_dma
